# A last line of defence, not a layout.
#
# The application is meant to live OUTSIDE the web root, with only the
# contents of public/ inside it — see DEPLOYMENT.md, step 3. If it has ended
# up inside public_html anyway, which is the easiest mistake to make on shared
# hosting, this file stops the web server handing out the shop's secrets.
#
# It costs nothing where the layout is right, because nothing ever asks the
# web server for these paths.

# The .env holds the database password, the Razorpay secret and the app key.
# A single request for it is the whole shop.
<FilesMatch "^\.env|^\.env\..*|composer\.(json|lock)|package(-lock)?\.json|artisan|phpunit\.xml|\.gitignore|\.gitattributes|.*\.(log|sqlite|sql|md|yml|yaml|sh)$">
    Require all denied
</FilesMatch>

# Source, configuration, migrations, tests and the vendor tree. None of it is
# meant to be read over HTTP; only public/ is.
RedirectMatch 404 ^/(app|bootstrap|config|database|resources|routes|storage|tests|vendor|node_modules)(/|$)

# Never list a directory that has no index.
Options -Indexes
